        "step1": {
          "title": "Going \"Fully React\" w/ Nikhil Saraf",
          "duration": "5:49:11",
          "channel": "Ryan Carniato",
          "description": "Nikhil Saraf, SolidJS Core Team member, and maintainer of SolidStart joins us to talk about what he's been doing lately. He has been busy implementing a fully featured React Server Component solution with routing, data fetching, and mutation on top of Vite, and he is going to share with us what he has learned.\n\n[0:00] Preamble\n[8:15] Welcome Nikhil Saraf\n[20:00] RSC Checklist - What Do We Need?\n[36:30] The Perils of Nested Data Fetching\n[50:15] Patching Global Fetch\n[1:02:00] Routing is Essential\n[1:18:30] \"Fully React\" - HN Example Code Walkthrough\n[1:36:30] Demos: HN Example\n[1:46:45] Kerplunk! - Caching and Pre-Loading\n[2:05:00] Server Entry\n[2:17:15] Client Entry\n[2:32:15] Demos: Simple Mutation Example\n[2:44:15] RSC - SPA or MPA?\n[2:58:00] Demos: SSG, Sessions, Auth, and Apple Music\n[3:13:30] Key Takeaways: Separation & Data Distance\n[3:32:00] Key Takeaways: Propietary Data Format\n[3:38:00] Key Takeaways: Directives vs. Decorators\n[3:45:00] Evaluating Solid Server Components\n[3:57:30] Q & A: Differences with React & Solid \n[4:10:15] Q & A: What Would You Change with RSC's?  \n[4:16:45] Current Status of SolidStart  \n[4:37:15] Nikhil's Parting Notes\n[4:47:15] This Week in JavaScript: Solid News \n[4:50:00] TWiJ: Rich Harris - IMHO\n[4:54:15] TWiJ: Dan Abramov - Colocation and RSC Quiz \n[5:07:45] TWiJ: Theo Browne - RSC Thoughts \n[5:19:00] TWiJ: Dan Abramov - Defending Fetch Patch\n[5:31:30] TWiJ: Ryan's Thoughts on React & Standards\n[5:38:30] TWiJ: Dave Di Biase - Svelte Super Fan\n[5:46:00] Conclusion\n\nThanks @zombiefacesupreme for the timestamps.",
